<urn:atm:triage:finding/CPR-007>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "CPR-007" ;
  triage:title "Escalation recipient read fails open: one unparseable stored row silently disables all oversight for the team" ;
  triage:description "Hostile closure review (general-purpose opus, task af4edaf6699568f49) @ 9f5aef2fe. Escalation recipient read fails open: one unparseable stored row silently disables all oversight for the team. Doc says: nudge-task-design.md §6.2: 'Addresses are free-form text, so `omega-prime@hermes` works today and a future `rand@human` needs no schema change.' Code does: crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/task_store.rs:389 now parses each stored recipient and returns Err on failure, erroring the whole scope. load_escalation_recipients catches that and substitutes an empty list: `Err(error) => { tracing::warn!(... outcome = 'failed' ...); Vec::new() }`. Recommendation: Skip and warn on the individual unparseable row rather than failing the scope, and never substitute an empty recipient list for a read error — escalate to the lead or surface a health error instead. Add tests for both arms. fenix's ruling: skip and warn on the individual unparseable recipient row rather than failing the whole scope; on a genuine read error, Hold with one warn per tick rather than silently substituting an empty recipient list." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_escalation.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix (ATM 01M2AAHXS8QB8CQTR4J0BSHVST, 2026-09-12T08:08:16Z): fixed at review-2 1afb11318. Gate-green confirmed (ATM 01M2AAP2C6BY2DSSEKEWX2S3YA, 2026-09-12T08:10:32Z) on fenix's host." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
